{"posts":[{"id":"3drive_p8_176","t":"\"would the pro traders here take such trades with low risk-reward?\" General rule regarding RR is that your trades should be at least 3:1 RR. On this forum you could quite often see trades 1:6, 1:7 or even 1:15. If you really want to be impressed check IF's journal where you can find 1:20 or 1:50 RR trades:P They are possible. I know that even from my experience (I think about 1:7 RR trades here).\n\nFrom reasons I gave you above I think that you shouldn't bother you with trades with 1:1 RR even if the PA confirm the trade. The trading opportunities are countless, but you money is not:)\n\n3:1 RR (and above) may save your account. I remember that 1,5 year ago I take one trade which was 1:10 RR and after that I have 8 losers in a row... Thanks to RR I was still earning money (I was +2 R).\n\nTorosar wrote: That is just the thing.. The true supply was within reach just above and a possibility of a fakeout is very real. If I were to enter on that 3drive my risk-reward would at best be 1:1. We know that price action validates the level but would the pro traders here take such trades with low risk-reward? BTW: 2 days wiser and indeed touching the true supply got us a great reaction to the downside.","a":"kkb","d":"","n":"#176","p":8,"im":[],"m":176},{"id":"3drive_p8_177","t":"Found a beauty, today.","a":"rcmacf","d":"","n":"#177","p":8,"im":["1d008dc7fcf2b9ec2825b1d45723377504daca57"],"m":177},{"id":"3drive_p8_178","t":"A 3 drive is just compression, isn't it. 3 drive, 4 drive 5 drive. It's all cp.","a":"Oedipus","d":"","n":"#178","p":8,"im":[],"m":178},{"id":"3drive_p8_179","t":"Yeah the more i'm studing charts the less i'm focusing on finding the perfect pattern...the simpler the better...it's all about eng-origin...and the CP cleans the way for price to shoot away","a":"Redbullish","d":"","n":"#179","p":8,"im":[],"m":179},{"id":"3drive_p8_180","t":"Hi guys!!This is my first post here. I'm not sure,but is it a really 3D? We want 1):fresh supply/demand for reaction. 2)compression at demand/supply 3)is the target at the base of compression??\n\nAny comments are much appreciated.Thank you","a":"full","d":"","n":"#180","p":8,"im":["d7ce4c0f32bb89a6ef7410cf2c1d28d86b66a872"],"m":180},{"id":"3drive_p8_181","t":"Hey Full, I am not sure why you are referring to the area as ignored h4 supply. To me, it seems to be an origin flag limit of the break of the last active low prior to the drop, which price returned to. I would say that it is rather obvious that price was in a big compression stage on return, which seem to have some drives on the way as you nicely pointed out. For me, I like to see 3 drives as we get close to the origins of significant areas in the past.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#181","p":8,"im":["a24f4c08b66156da7508a27c593016e964fdc67d"],"m":181},{"id":"3drive_p8_182","t":"Hi naascott:Thank you for the reply. I don't understand why the area in the chart it's not a interesting area. I understood in your chart,that the decision point engulf the flag limit end then become the source of the down move. am I right?","a":"full","d":"","n":"#182","p":8,"im":["5b99d1ee7132d67b00462425745d88695fd30e66"],"m":182},{"id":"3drive_p8_183","t":"Hey Full,\n\nIt is a most interesting area, indeed! A great place to begin looking for shorts. I was just a little unsure what was meant by the statement of ignored supply - that's all. Had you stated that previously ignored demand became supply, then I would have got what you meant right away. Now I see what you meant. For this particular area, seeing the RS, I would look for the obvious FL around it. I then would wait to see what price does when it comes back. And seeing the 3-D on approach on the lower time frame was a nice part of the confirmation.","a":"naascott","d":"","n":"#183","p":8,"im":[],"m":183},{"id":"3drive_p8_184","t":"Hey Naascott!!and this??","a":"full","d":"","n":"#184","p":8,"im":["807b7a87e1a9a086ecbb23c50124cd8b18882302"],"m":184},{"id":"3drive_p8_185","t":"Hey Full,\n\nHere are some of my observations on the chart. I didn't check the HTF on this but if the QM was in HTF demand it would be a safe bet to take it after the engulf showed up. Since we didn't have an engulf higher, (the leg up reacted off the QM of the previous leg down) I wouldn't have taken a Touch Trade there.\n\nThe reaction off the QM is good but we failed to get back to the top. Seems like we made it just past the flip zone in the stacked supply down.\n\nYour ignored demand can be tightened up a bit where I put the number 1. There is a FL on this TF that holds price down then after a few tests from underneath price ignores it and shoots through (didn't check M1 on this) you can see the reaction to this zone when we engulf. Which is also a smaller cap retest and QM.\n\nHope this helps some. You're doing well with your analysis. Cheers","a":"antraxia","d":"","n":"#185","p":8,"im":["f8c859f7e2ea370beb8a020385d8046e9a585e11","fea0c41ee229fa2417c5c18437af16ca03437f12"],"m":185},{"id":"3drive_p8_186","t":"Hi Antraxia!!Thank you for reply.. I completely agree whit you.We didn't have an engulf higher (for QM) But,when I Drew ignored D become S become D. I have noted an FO (possible quasimodo on M5??) In your chart you market Engulf Cap retest.I based the possible trade in that analysis.. (details in the chart) How do you rate this trade??","a":"full","d":"","n":"#186","p":8,"im":["62fa9899314cd9a1af0e82431726ba45c0d03a2b"],"m":186},{"id":"3drive_p8_187","t":"Looks good from over here Full. Again I would see if the QM is in HTF Demand to strengthen this trade. If not, I would expect it to bounce at the next FL and move my stop aggressively.\n\nThis is a trade I would definitely take. You have room up to the next FL after the first engulf and your risk is kept really low (below the last FL) or below the QM bottom for a chance to get to BE at least and much more if you make it up to the full target. You are given warning of the reversal by the small 3 drive. Keep practicing! Cheers.","a":"antraxia","d":"","n":"#187","p":8,"im":["f8c859f7e2ea370beb8a020385d8046e9a585e11"],"m":187},{"id":"3drive_p8_188","t":"Away\n\nThis is my homework on 3 drive","a":"lv5758","d":"","n":"#188","p":8,"im":["f7189829b0c5d499cbe41b56ed5f24a8c0d32aa1"],"m":188},{"id":"3drive_p8_189","t":"Hey, this is my first homework on the 3 drive. They are no beauties, but I guess this is not necessary to work:)","a":"thetrendsfriend","d":"","n":"#189","p":8,"im":["47e417659818162efefdf355baecbd9c61d84677","4f9549c7bed7bd3bceb81ff9a17320439fab1ae3"],"m":189},{"id":"3drive_p8_190","t":"Another two...","a":"thetrendsfriend","d":"","n":"#190","p":8,"im":["9e3267751afe3d67d267777df924029bf5accf01","0db78849ce671c59b47120bf4f91eb7b42a9acb6"],"m":190},{"id":"3drive_p8_191","t":"Hi All,\n\nAttached is my 3Drive homework.\n\nAs I'm new to this I would really appreciate anyone taking the time to let me know if I'm doing this correctly.\n\nTheir was a lot more that I could have added but I dramatically reduced the selection by only using 3Drive where I could see clear CP in 1 and in most cases also in 2.\n\nThanks a mill","a":"Tirnanog","d":"","n":"#191","p":8,"im":["4affe7d3fcbff9aa864be7a3aba50cc7ad765eb5","fcd338b5f349ceaf7a292d8b7cf6f0a830849696","8c46f8b9360f9f78ce4ea2b0ec56d5064dd1ec19","cd776d87b54e20ef54754f39811a9b0d97b2c21e","0819128b2940d801bd589ad9e989d5f8f5b82c2d","f24104a4fe6a35a22f2669bd3fe1f8703628f510","47b61f5ab75de9c05b969d0b2e1cc8fb08389166","d70b14989e19a3d86f0556ed25b8b9b9c4e48ae6","297129ba0109cae6999c36b1cef53aba9c5af184","d41346a46be0345efc8a617f4a7d7777bbd105d2","1868d5778e26b29dbf997dd2aa200462cdedc0f5","bf3417059864127f6fb8cb26a5d4b34e0bb6d150","26c751a59689c94a64639c8180e387670e4e72ad","30a5e047552e0a9ecc081a231f415bebc27184d5","77ad497ff571fb2a3612f416e1f622ef4194f1ab","4f7c1ccb328bdd0d9c3adbc57d0b4aab15d8d4e4"],"m":191},{"id":"3drive_p8_192","t":"Away\n\nYa it didn't worked, since you can see market traded in sideway fo